# Build context for the combined VanFlow suite image.
#
# The context is the PARENT of the three projects, because one image needs all
# three sources. That parent also holds unrelated repos and ~GB of build output,
# so this file is deny-by-default: ignore everything, then re-admit only the
# three project directories, then strip their heavy subdirectories.
#
# Without the deny-by-default first line the context was several gigabytes —
# ERP/integration-hub alone is 630 MB of node_modules and .next.
*

!ERP/
!cash-van-dashboard/
!cash-van-dashboard-frontend/

# The entrypoint lives at the context root, so deny-by-default excludes it too.
# Missing this failed the build at the COPY with a bare "not found".
!suite-entrypoint.sh

# Re-admitted above, now strip what must never enter an image: dependencies are
# installed inside the build, and build output is produced there.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.git
**/.gradle
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# A whole second Next.js app sitting untracked inside the ERP working tree.
ERP/integration-hub

# Local-only and secret-bearing files. An .env baked into an image is a
# credential shipped to whoever can pull it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.DS_Store
**/.claude
**/*.log

# Runtime data, anchored to the exact directories that hold it.
#
# These were once written as **/storage and **/uploads, which match ANY path
# segment with that name — and so silently excluded three SOURCE directories:
# cash-van-dashboard/src/common/storage (the StorageService itself, which failed
# the build with "Cannot find module"), ERP/src/app/api/uploads, and
# cash-van-dashboard-frontend/fe-academy/.../storage. A bare ** glob on a common
# word will eventually match source; anchor it.
/cash-van-dashboard/storage
/ERP/public/uploads
